# Managed harness sources and the manifest that records their hashes are pinned
# to LF in every checkout. SHA-256 is byte-sensitive: with `core.autocrlf=true`
# an unpinned checkout would rewrite every managed byte to CRLF and none of the
# tracked manifest hashes would match. These rules keep the checkout, the Git
# blob, and the manifest byte-identical on Windows, macOS, and Linux.
baseline/** text eol=lf
manifest/*.json text eol=lf
# The routing contract is inserted verbatim into wiki/index.md, so its bytes
# must match on every machine that patches or verifies that section.
contracts/*.md text eol=lf
